 "notes": "Side view, facing east, unmirrored (No.10 is right-footed: the near/right leg touches). Points are pixel indices (studioAnim adds 0.5; contact lands on the bottom edge of row 102). Ground frames sit on contact = the planted boot's toe-tip column on row 102 (Settle F1: the braking right heel); airborne frames (contact null) sit on pelvis. ball = centre of the 12 px ball (radius 6 at x1; r 12 at x2, r 18 at x3), NEVER drawn in the frame; touch = the boot is on the ball; boot = the contact pixel of bootPart on the drawn boot; head = skull point; eye = the pupil pixel (measured); lowBoot = lowest pixel of an airborne frame; bbox = [x0,y0,x1,y1] measured on the art. solo = SPOTLIGHT SOLO shot-local use times. Studio layer: Art only (no Num/Ball layer; the ball guide is these anchors). Dribble (75 ms, studio 13 fps): right stance F2-F5 on the right toe-tip (73,102), left stance F6-F8,F1 on the left toe-tip (76,102). originDx = world x of each canvas from the cycle F1 (F1 0, F2-F5 24, F6-F8 42; the cycle advances 42 px = 70 px/s at x1): the shot-2 scroll and the field scroll must equal it so the feet never slide. Ball rolls on row 96 and is touched on F1 (right laces) and F5 (left instep). Shot 4 closing (Dribble F2-F4 at the cycle origin +70 after SoleLift F11, polish 2026-11-15): use each frame's `ballByUse` ('s4 1.85' / 's4 1.90' / 's4 1.95', canvas px = world C +70: 145.5,92 / 152.5,95.5 / 160.5,96) instead of the cycle `ball`: the cushioned ball rolls off the instep over the planted right toe onto the turf (the cycle anchors popped it 9.6 px forward + 5 px down at 1.85). The cycle `ball` stays for shots 2/7 and the field. F2/F6: the trailing toe peels off its planted column (3 px up), no slide.",
